Digital game ownership has been a revolutionary advancement in the industry which allowed users to access games without a physcial disc or cartridge copy through an online serbice. For example, on playstation this service and the players access to their product is dependant on Sonys online service to verify their licence whenever they want to use it, this creates a lot of controversy around owning the product you bought and the level of access you truly have to it. There is also concern around if a game is released with issues or bugs that need fixing it can only be fixed through online updates that might not be available to someone with no access to wifi

#Cloud Gaming
Cloud gaming is another service that has been becoming more available in recent years and it provides users with a way to access video games without needing to own hardware to run it on themselves, this removes
the barrier of expensive gaming hardware thats needed to play some big titles at an enjoyable performance and speed. The games are ran similarly to how netflix and other streaming services work where the file of the game 
is on another machine elsewhere and depends on your own wifi to use these machines. However this can make the users wifi the new hardware issue

#Hardware Failures
When people used to mainly go to the arcade to play video games, machines would occasionally go out of order for hardware or software related reasons. If this happened it was not too much of a concern to the players as the arcade would be responsible for servicing and repairing the machines, with the move to home gaming hardware failures became more of a concern. A lot of consoles made in the 80s and 90s such as the NES, Sega and playstation systems were engineered well and functionally held up well past warranty, but when the xbox 360 first released it had a very common fatal hardware failure on most consoles called the red ring of death. This left a mark on microsofts reputation as it left most people who had spent hundreds on the new console with a useless and completely disfunctional piece of technology. Microsoft fought this issue by replacing the broken consoles and the issue would keep on occurring even with new models. This greatly affected everyone who owned a 360 in its early days and went on to make companies work more to prevent this from happening again. 

